{start_of_verse}
[D]With every golden curl in place she’s as [G]fine as Queen Anne’s [D]lace
And know one could ever fault the way she [A]looks tonight
The man [D]standing by her side shows her [G]off with such eager [D]pride
Seems since I saw her [A]last she’s done all [D]right
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[D]She could never place me in her mind for me the [G]years have not been [D]kind
[D]She’d never see the boy she knew in the [A]man I’ve grown to be
From [D]her station and her place she’d never [G]recognize my [D]face
I have fallen like a wind blown [A]leaf from her [D]memory
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For she’s [G]traded all her pain for bright [D]lights and chilled champayne
[D]And I’m sure her new found friends all think they [A]know just where she’s been
Yes they [D]think they know here well all the [G]stories I could [D]tell
She’s as fine as Queen Anne’s [A]lace but I knew her [D]when
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Now it’s hard to believe I know but she once [G]loved me long [D]ago
And I ‘spose I should be hurtin’ just to [A]see her once again
Oh but [D]now she’s grown so proud I wouldn’t [G]want her [D]anyhow
She’s as fine as Queen Anne’s [A]lace but I knew her [D]when
{end_of_verse}

